# Standalone template checkout: when this clean template becomes the root of its own Git
# repository, the complete tree — including this .gitattributes and every descendant —
# checks out LF on every platform so the 151-file release ledger is byte-deterministic
# regardless of core.autocrlf. `text=auto` keeps a future binary asset from being
# corrupted; this is a scoped LF contract, not a blanket byte rewrite.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The generated navigation read model must stay LF on every platform so its bytes
# match the standard-library generator's output (scripts/generate_okf_navigation.py)
# and `--check` stays deterministic regardless of core.autocrlf.
08_pkg/generated/okf_navigation.md text eol=lf

# OKF/profile byte boundary: the reusable framework-profile contract, public API
# contract, authoring guide, dependency metadata, profile checker/adapter, and the
# full golden-fixture corpus check out LF on every platform so their bytes stay
# stable under core.autocrlf=true or false. Explicit boundary rules — not a
# repository-wide EOL rewrite.
08_pkg/okf_profile_v0_1.md text eol=lf
08_pkg/public_api_contract.md text eol=lf
docs/template_framework/okf_authoring_and_migration.md text eol=lf
pyproject.toml text eol=lf
